# 💰 Personal Finance API

A **robust and scalable backend API** built with **Node.js, Express, Prisma, and PostgreSQL** for managing personal finances.
This system allows users to track income and expenses, manage budgets, and gain financial insights through analytics.

---

## 🚀 Overview

The **Personal Finance API** is designed to help users:

* Track income and expenses
* Organize transactions using categories
* Set monthly budgets
* Analyze financial data through dashboards

The project follows **clean architecture principles** and demonstrates real-world backend development practices including authentication, validation, and optimized database design.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

* **Node.js** – Runtime environment
* **Express.js** – Web framework
* **Prisma ORM** – Database ORM
* **PostgreSQL** – Relational database
* **JWT (JSON Web Token)** – Authentication
* **Bcrypt** – Password hashing
* **Swagger (OpenAPI)** – API documentation

---

## 📦 Features

### 🔐 Authentication

* User registration & login
* Secure password hashing
* JWT-based authentication
* Protected routes

---

### 💰 Transactions

* Create, read, and delete transactions
* Supports:

  * Income
  * Expenses
* Filtering:

  * By type
  * By category
  * By date range
* Pagination & sorting

---

### 🗂️ Categories

* Default (global) categories
* User-defined categories
* Category-based transaction organization

---

### 💸 Budget Management

* Set monthly budgets per category
* Update or delete budgets
* Prevent duplicate budget entries per month

---

### 📊 Analytics Dashboard

* Total income
* Total expenses
* Current balance
* Category-based expense breakdown
* Monthly financial trends

---

### 📚 API Documentation

* Interactive Swagger UI
* Available at:

```
/api/docs
```

---

## 🧱 Project Structure

```
src/
 ├── controllers/      # Handle HTTP requests
 ├── services/         # Business logic
 ├── routes/           # API routes
 ├── middlewares/      # Auth & error handling
 ├── validators/       # Request validation
 ├── prisma/           # Prisma schema & client
 ├── utils/            # Helper functions
 ├── config/           # Config files (Swagger, env)
 ├── app.js            # Express app setup
 └── server.js         # Entry point
```

---

## ⚙️ Setup Instructions

### 1️⃣ Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/personal-finance-api.git
cd personal-finance-api
```

---

### 2️⃣ Install dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

---

### 3️⃣ Setup environment variables

Create a `.env` file:

```env
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/personal_finance"
JWT_SECRET="your_secret_key"
PORT=5000
```

---

### 4️⃣ Setup database

Run Prisma migration:

```bash
npx prisma migrate dev --name init
```

---

### 5️⃣ Seed default categories (optional)

```bash
node src/prisma/seed.js
```

---

### 6️⃣ Run the server

```bash
npm run dev
```

Server will run at:

```
http://localhost:5000
```

---

## 🔐 Authentication

All protected routes require a JWT token:

```
Authorization: Bearer <your_token>
```

---

## 📡 API Endpoints (Overview)

### Auth

* `POST /api/auth/register`
* `POST /api/auth/login`

---

### Transactions

* `GET /api/transactions`
* `POST /api/transactions`
* `DELETE /api/transactions/:id`

---

### Categories

* `GET /api/categories`
* `POST /api/categories`
* `DELETE /api/categories/:id`

---

### Budgets

* `GET /api/budgets`
* `POST /api/budgets`
* `DELETE /api/budgets/:id`

---

### Analytics

* `GET /api/analytics/summary`
* `GET /api/analytics/category`
* `GET /api/analytics/monthly`

---

